{"toolCallId":"call_689b0230c8f04be489b686be71223ca6","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"total 41\nFILE_EXISTS | error |  | Validates required spec documents for the declared documentation level.\nSCAFFOLD_NEVER_TOUCHED | error |  | Rejects scaffold-signature markers in required docs when spec.md claims Complete status.\nLEVEL_DECLARED | info |  | Reports whether the documentation level was declared or inferred.\nAC_COVERAGE | info |  | Default-on advisory (non-blocking) scan for acceptance-criteria traceability coverage; set SPECKIT_AC_COVERAGE=false to opt out.\nAC_CLOSURE | error |  | Gates packet closure on acceptance-criteria.md at Levels 2, 3 and 3+; unmet criteria block a completion claim and a waiver must cite an ADR that exists. Packets created before the cutoff stay advisory.\nCOMPLEXITY_MATCH | error |  | Checks declared level against content complexity signals.\nFRONTMATTER_VALID | error |  | Validates YAML frontmatter structure and required semantic values.\nLEVEL_MATCH | error |  | Checks required files match the declared documentation level.\nGRAPH_METADATA_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates graph-metadata.json shape: required packet/derived blocks, last_active_child_id pointer integrity for phase parents.\nDESCRIPTION_SHAPE | warn |  | Validates description.json shape: required name/description/level keys present and well-typed.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_ROOT_SPEC_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include a root spec reference.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_SOURCE_DOCS_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical saves include source document references.\nCANONICAL_SAVE_LINEAGE_REQUIRED | error |  | Ensures canonical save lineage metadata is present.\nCONTINUITY_FRESHNESS | error | strict | Strict-mode freshness check for continuity frontmatter. The rule reports warn by default and escalates to fail under SPECKIT_COMPLETION_FRESHNESS_ENFORCE; the ceiling here has to allow that escalation, since a warn ceiling would silently cap it.\nGENERATED_METADATA_INTEGRITY | error | strict | Validates description.json and graph-metadata.json through the shared schemas plus path-prefix and status-enum invariants, error under strict behind a grandfather report mode.\nGENERATED_METADATA_DRIFT | error | strict | Re-derives a folder and reports drift between the stored description/causal_summary and the current docs, read-only, error under strict only when the drift-gate flag is on and otherwise grandfather report mode.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"717a2b","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
