{"toolCallId":"call_86b554a9f7d449769f78cb537b9c8d20","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/acceptance-criteria.md:63:| AC-010 | REQ-009 | Given a run that writes a warning to stderr while `--quiet` is set, When the script runs, Then the warning is still written to stderr and stdout holds only the level line | Capturing stderr separately with `2>stderr.txt` leaves the warning line in the stderr capture, and `wc -l` on the stdout capture prints 1 | Unmet | - |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/spec.md:94:| REQ-009 | With `--quiet`, any warning the script writes to stderr is still written to stderr, so `--quiet` trims stdout only. |\nspecs/zz-bench-authoring/001-recommend-level-quiet-flag/tasks.md:50:- [ ] T017 Keep every stderr warning on stderr when `--quiet` is set, so the flag trims stdout only (REQ-009) (recommend-level.sh)\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w4fbf614733/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"280f2f","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
